# A cable pull for Phase 1a, step 8 (docs/roadmap.md): pull the output
# device's USB cable mid-playback, wait about 10 seconds, and plug it back in.
#
#     ks-harness --channels 4 src/apps/harness/scripts/cable-pull.harness
#
# Deck 1 sweeps up three octaves over two minutes (40 seconds an octave), so
# its pitch tells you where it is. While the cable is out the engine keeps its
# clock running, so when the output comes back the sweep is higher by the time
# it was gone (10 s is about 3 semitones), rather than carrying on from where
# it stopped. Deck 2 clicks once a second, on the headphone bus only.
#
# The harness prints "Freewheeling" when it notices the loss and "Playing"
# when it's back on the device. At the end, "Played" should be about 120 s
# and "Device losses: 1".

track sweep sweep 110 880 120 rate 44100
track tick clicks 60 120 rate 48000

0 main -6
0 headphones -12
0 load 1 sweep
0 play 1
0 load 2 tick
0 play 2
0 fader 2 0
0 pfl 2 on

120 end
